  "exceptions": [
    "initial, repeat, changed, force and failure facets are covered by the listed scenarios.",
    "An admitted trigger rewrites the settings row with the same value, so a no-subscriber trigger leaves the document value unchanged but moves the row updatedAt; the scenario asserts the value, not the timestamp.",
    "Queue saturation and ordering under concurrent triggers are not asserted: the manager serialises triggers with a one second delay and stores only eventName/eventData in the queue, so a queued ?fail trigger loses its override; the packet waits for each trigger event instead of racing the queue."
